From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix automake conditional append swallowed as recipe

Upstream indents the conditional SUBDIRS append with a TAB:

  if HAVE_MAKEINFO
  	SUBDIRS += doc
  endif

automake does not parse TAB-indented assignments, so it passes the
line through literally as "@HAVE_MAKEINFO_TRUE@<TAB>SUBDIRS += doc".
In the generated Makefile that line lands right after the
".PRECIOUS: Makefile" rule, where GNU make reads the TAB-prefixed
line as that rule's recipe instead of a variable append.  The doc
subdirectory (the user manual) is then silently never built nor
installed even when makeinfo is present.

Use a space-indented append, which automake handles via its
conditional mechanism.

--- a/guile-dbi/Makefile.am
+++ b/guile-dbi/Makefile.am
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 
 SUBDIRS = libltdl src include
 if HAVE_MAKEINFO
-	SUBDIRS += doc
+SUBDIRS += doc
 endif
 
 MAKEFLAGS = --no-print-directory
